---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About · Ahmad Abdillah">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Who is talking.</h1>
    <!--
      Identity page: says who is talking so essays do not have to.
      Decide consciously before publishing:
      - how much real-world identity lives here (name is already committed by the domain)
      - whether ThreatUnpacked gets a cross-link from here, or stays fully separate
      - nothing about employer, tooling specifics, or anything interview-hostile
    -->
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am Ahmad Abdillah. By day I work in security incident response: reading
        systems under stress, tracing how they break. The rest of the time I read,
        write, and try to do both with ihsan.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site holds the personal voice: essays on deen, craft, and the machine,
        plus shorter notes and a reading log. The technical research lives elsewhere,
        and stays there.
      </p>
      <p>The fastest way to follow along is the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) 4rem; }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
</style>
